Bad idea.  Anyway, if marvin was banned, I have a hunch that we'd see a 
mysterious "nivram" person appear to win the same trophies...

The problem with your current system is that there aren't enough interesting 
categories to compete in, and no runners-up or objective trophies.  For 
instance, there is only one slot that rewards fast ascension.  Players who 
can't do it in less than 15k turns have no hope at all, and so should ignore 
the turn counter entirely, because turn count doesn't matter for *anything* 
else.  Similarly, only one slot exists to reward conducts; if you can't do 
at least seven, you are wasting your time trying any.

Virtually all the non-junk awards are for putting together long strings of 
ascensions (I'll ignore the huge cheating possibilities currently present in 
this category because they *could* be fixed).  These require both very high 
ascension rates and plenty of free time.  The vast majority of players -- 
even good players -- don't have those, so they might as well stop playing 
after getting their D. Star or Birdie.  

How I would do it:
- Give 1 point (as a base) for each and *every* ascension.
- Dump the Dilithium Star.
- Dump the "Birdie" as irrelevant.
- Reduce the point values of the "Double Top", because the player is already 
being compensated for the ascensions which compose it.
- Reduce the point value of Most Ascensions, for the same reason.
- Reduce the point value of the "Hat Trick" for the same reason, and also 
because the player has certainly already earned the "Double Top".
- Modify the "Grand Slam" to not require all races; the player will probably 
also earn the "Hat Trick", but he shouldn't be forced to.  The current point 
value (6) seems fair, because one ascension from each class is certainly 
harder than 13 Valks.
- Dump the High Score: Class trophies.
- Reduce the Highest Scored Ascension award to 2 points.
- Reduce the grue challenge point award to .5 (at best).
- Modify the Elbereth challenge so it has an in-game solution which no 
longer involves KoL at all, and cut the point award to .3 or so.

And reward conducts with multipliers applied to the base one point earned 
for an ascension:

Vegetarian - 110%
Vegan      - 110% (not significantly harder than vegetarian) 
Foodless   - 200%
Atheist    - 125%
Weaponless - 105% (could be 120% for non-Monks)
Pacifist   - 200%
Illiterate - 120%
Genocide   - 110%
Polypile   - 120%
Polyself   - 100% (not a meaningful challenge)
Wishless   - 150%
Artiwish   - 105% (most people keep this anyway)

And reward speed:
 < 10k turns  - 200%
10k-15k turns - 170%
15k-20k turns - 150%
20k-25k turns - 130%
25k-30k turns - 115%
30k-40k turns - 105%
 > 40k turns  - 100%

The standard Geno-Poly-Polyself-Wishless combination in 22k turns would be 
worth 2.574 points (1.0 x 110% x 120% x 100% x 150% x 130%)



